  "summary": "I'm a recent college graduate of computer science with a background in mobile and game development. I'm proficient in the Objective-C language as well as C#, Swift, and C++.  I have worked on several personal projects as well as production level code at my internship with Jack henry & Associates. The platforms for these projects have given me skills in IDE's such as Xcode, Visual Studio, MonoDevelop as well as the Unity3D game engine.\n\nI developed most of my skills in mobile development at Jack Henry & Associates where I have been for the past year and a half. During my first summer with the company, I was put though a rigorous IOS development boot camp where I learned Objective-C, Swift, Cocoa Touch, Core Data, and common IOS design patterns. Currently, I'm working with the full-time engineers refactoring parts of the teams large code base, fixing bugs, and adding new features to the application.\n\nMost of my game development skills were acquired over hobby/school projects using the Unity3D game engine along with the C# language. I published a mobile game using Unity3D in 2015 called Angus the Dwarf to both IOS and Android platforms. Since then, I have worked on many hobby projects using both 2D and 3D graphics as well as VR/AR platform based. During my senior project while at Missouri State University, I led a team to work on a mobile virtual reality project using Unity3D.\n\nI'm currently looking for a position in either the mobile or game development field. I can be reached through this profile and usually respond within a few days.",
